{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>The firstborn according to his birthright.</b> Rashi explained: when he reached Benjamin he said, 'this one has no mother,' etc. Joseph thought his father's wives were still alive." "<b>And they were astonished.</b> Perforce the astonishment was not at their being seated before him, the firstborn according to his birthright, since it is not written ויושיבם but <b>וישבו</b> — they sat down of themselves. Rather, they were astonished at what they saw: he set portions for him by himself and for them by themselves and for the Egyptians by themselves. They said: what is the nature of this one, that since he eats apart — he is neither Egyptian nor Hebrew?"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:32.679881104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}